  "description": "The temple of the god Adad, Enamhe (\u201cHouse of Plenty\u201d), was located in the Kumar district of Babylon, in the western half of the inner city. According to the Babylonian topographical text Tintir = Babylon Tablet IV, it was one of seven temples in that part of Babylon. Enamhe was (re)built by the the Old Babylonian kings S\u016bm\u00fb-l\u0101-El (r. ca. 1881\u20131845 BC) and Hammu-r\u0101pi (r. ca. 1792\u20131750 BC) and the Neo-Babylonian ruler Nebuchadnezzar II (r. 604\u2013562 BC).",
